{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564978-so-how-would-you-feel-if-the-hypothetical-w6-abandon-a-fixed-setting","id":1564978,"title":"So how would you feel if the hypothetical W6 abandon a fixed setting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-10-26T06:03:20-07:00","id":1564978,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> So how would you feel if the hypothetical W6 abandon a fixed setting?","content":"So let's assume that WoD 6e survived past M&amp;C 6. And White Wolf subsequently decided they should take a different approach please everyone for (or maybe shortly before) W6 rather than V6 style Canon reset.<br /> <br /> Basically White Wolf have w6 discard with any pretense of a fixed setting/metaplot to a even greater extent than the heavy pared back setting of W5. Somewhat like the later books in the chronicles of darkness.<br /> <br /> Though maybe a bit of mechanical framework and genral organisation so the ST has an easier time to set up they own version of WtA.<br /> <br /> An example writing up a series of presets on the default state of the garou nation (Mainly weather it's fallen or not) and giving tribes a of alternative states (with the cult being a extreme deviation) connected via a flow chart akin to HOI focus parths.<br /> <br /> Effectively making the W6 source book into a narrative Lego set for a ST to put together rather than a pre-made setting primer. With supplements adding more pieces to the lego set such as going into detail on the alternative parths that the tribes can take and more setting elements like the fera.<br /> <br /> Like would this be a good idea for W6?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T06:35:20-07:00","id":1564979,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t like that. I buy WoD books mostly for setting and lore, which is why I prefer World of Darkness to Chronicles of Darkness (that as well as the greater complexity of Chronicles). That would make me a lot less likely to buy a new edition of Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T17:51:39-07:00","id":1564995,"title":"","content":"I'd rather play Forsaken, then. Which, for this proposal, is just better and already established.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-27T19:30:28-07:00","id":1565009,"title":"","content":"one of the big problems with open settings is it puts a ton on the storyteller/GM to figure out in order to run a game, which raises the barrier for getting people to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-27T19:52:55-07:00","id":1565010,"title":"","content":"It would be a damn sight better than what we actually ended up getting with W5.<br /> <br /> Though it could also be interpreted as laziness on the developer's part. Basically having them tell the players to make up their own narrative, rather than expand upon the decades of lore the previous editions had built up.<br /> <br /> I didn't mind the fact that Chronicles had no established meta plot, but that's because Chronicles was always meant from the beginning to be its own separate game line. It wasn't continuing the story of WoD, but rather it was rebooting the setting from the ground up.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12161\" data-vbnamecard=\"12161\">Browman</a> True, the ST would be required to either come up with a lot of world building in advance, or else try to make it up as they went.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-27T20:37:55-07:00","id":1565014,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the lack of setting on principle because it is a valid game proposal with its own target audience.<br /> <br /> The problem is that we already have a setting whose selling point was the lore, <i><u><b>and</b></u></i> a setting whose selling point is the solid structure upon which to use a toolbox approach.<br /> <br /> Doing this would be to take Apocalypse, strip it of everything that makes it Apocalypse, just to turn it into a discount version of Forsaken, that is already theirs so... Da fuck!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-27T21:38:23-07:00","id":1565016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564978-so-how-would-you-feel-if-the-hypothetical-w6-abandon-a-fixed-setting?p=1565014#post1565014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doing this would be to take Apocalypse, strip it of everything that makes it Apocalypse, just to turn it into a discount version of Forsaken, that is already theirs so... Da fuck!?</div> </div> </div> </div>They already did that. It's called <i>'Werewolf the Apocalypse: 5th edition!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-28T15:25:07-07:00","id":1565025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564978-so-how-would-you-feel-if-the-hypothetical-w6-abandon-a-fixed-setting#post1564978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let's assume that WoD 6e survived past M&amp;C 6. And White Wolf subsequently decided they should take a different approach please everyone for (or maybe shortly before) W6 rather than V6 style Canon reset.<br /> <br /> Basically White Wolf have w6 discard with any pretense of a fixed setting/metaplot to a even greater extent than the heavy pared back setting of W5. Somewhat like the later books in the chronicles of darkness.<br /> <br /> Though maybe a bit of mechanical framework and genral organisation so the ST has an easier time to set up they own version of WtA.<br /> <br /> An example writing up a series of presets on the default state of the garou nation (Mainly weather it's fallen or not) and giving tribes a of alternative states (with the cult being a extreme deviation) connected via a flow chart akin to HOI focus parths.<br /> <br /> Effectively making the W6 source book into a narrative Lego set for a ST to put together rather than a pre-made setting primer. With supplements adding more pieces to the lego set such as going into detail on the alternative parths that the tribes can take and more setting elements like the fera.<br /> <br /> Like would this be a good idea for W6?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unironically and without insult intended, isn't this what Forsaken is? Form-a-Fera workshop, wherein you build your own metaplot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-28T16:51:22-07:00","id":1565026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564978-so-how-would-you-feel-if-the-hypothetical-w6-abandon-a-fixed-setting?p=1565025#post1565025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unironically and without insult intended, isn't this what Forsaken is? Form-a-Fera workshop, wherein you build your own metaplot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... but the <i>&quot;Form-a-Fera workshop&quot;</i> was horrendously written,and had never even heard of the phrase <i>&quot;gameplay balance.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> To clarify, I'm talking about the CoD C<b>hanging Breeds</b> book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-28T18:44:00-07:00","id":1565027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564978-so-how-would-you-feel-if-the-hypothetical-w6-abandon-a-fixed-setting?p=1565026#post1565026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes... but the <i>&quot;Form-a-Fera workshop&quot;</i> was horrendously written,and had never even heard of the phrase <i>&quot;gameplay balance.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> To clarify, I'm talking about the CoD C<b>hanging Breeds</b> book.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole of it was a poorly-expanded version of War Against the Pure, and duplicated a measure of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-28T21:31:58-07:00","id":1565029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564978-so-how-would-you-feel-if-the-hypothetical-w6-abandon-a-fixed-setting?p=1565027#post1565027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The whole of it was a poorly-expanded version of War Against the Pure, and duplicated a measure of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also probably didn't hep there was virtually zero communication between writers and authors, since there are times when the book contradicts itself.<br /> <br /> Like how it tells us the Changing Breeds are not influenced by cultural or ethnic backgrounds, but then also goes on to tell us every single Wererat is of Indian stock.<br /> <br /> Also, whoever drew the ultra muscular Weredeer also made an uncensored version of the image, where the guy has his genitals fully exposed; and if you squint hard enough, you can also see a blurred set of genitals on one of the Weredog images.<br /> <br /> Then there was the Wereraven having breasts in their war form. Like, why does an avian need to have boobs when going into battle?<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, combine that with the fact the other Changing Breeds weren't forbidden to mate with each other, it seems like the book may have been written by a bunch of horny furries.<br /> <br /> Which, I mean... I'm one too, but this was a professionally commissioned project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 10-29-2026, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-29T18:19:05-07:00","id":1565043,"title":"","content":"I don't think the possibility of crossbreeding is a problem, but my disagreement ends there.<br /> <br /> The very notion of personal totemic animal that turns you into a were thing is weirdly out of pace with the rest of CoD. Or how it ignores the whole toolbox approach to adopt the old ecoterrorists default.<br /> <br /> Also goes to lengths to say they have nothing to do with human cultural expectations on the animal, then proceed to make every single one into a pastiche, up to the Devil-Goat, because nothing says &quot;human culture isn't a factor&quot; more than copying Christian iconography.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-29T18:44:25-07:00","id":1565044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564978-so-how-would-you-feel-if-the-hypothetical-w6-abandon-a-fixed-setting?p=1565043#post1565043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the possibility of crossbreeding is a problem, but my disagreement ends there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry, I meant mating between Shapeshifters in general. Since when two werewolves have a child, they create a monster that tries to kill them when it grows up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-29T18:59:02-07:00","id":1565046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564978-so-how-would-you-feel-if-the-hypothetical-w6-abandon-a-fixed-setting?p=1565044#post1565044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, sorry, I meant mating between Shapeshifters in general. Since when two werewolves have a child, they create a monster that tries to kill them when it grows up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in CoD.<br /> <br /> In Forsaken they just have a child that I don't remember now if they're always Uratha or just more frequently Uratha and otherwise Wolf blooded.<br /> <br /> But in WoD mating between species has no meaningful effect, there's no barrier.<br /> <br /> And even within the same Changing Breed it's not a hard rule, it varies by breed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 10-29-2026, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-29T21:30:44-07:00","id":1565047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564978-so-how-would-you-feel-if-the-hypothetical-w6-abandon-a-fixed-setting?p=1565046#post1565046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not in CoD.<br /> <br /> In Forsaken they just have a child that I don't remember now if they're always Uratha or just more frequently Uratha and otherwise Wolf blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Must have been removed in 2nd edition, then.<br /> <br /> In first edition, mating between two werewolves produces a spiritual wolf monster who immediately runs off into the spirit world as soon as it's born. If it's allowed to grow to maturity, it then comes back and begins a killing spree.<br /> <br /> Also, because it's a fully spiritual creature, instead of half flesh, it is invisible to mundane means of detection. So this thing could just show up and maul you without you even sensing it.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, basically an even worse punishment than the creation of a Metis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 10-30-2026, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}